---
title: "Drawbridge — Zero-trust fleet identity: the permission matrix is a deliverable, not config"
---
flowchart LR
  subgraph FLEET["FIVE AGENT IDENTITIES — no shared credential exists anywhere in the fleet"]
    direction TB
    SA1["<b>sa-orchestrator</b>"]
    SA2["<b>sa-questionnaire</b>"]
    SA3["<b>sa-evidence</b>"]
    SA4["<b>sa-scorer</b>"]
    SA5["<b>sa-watchdog</b>"]
  end

  G1["Firestore state read and write<br/>Pub/Sub publish and subscribe<br/>Vertex AI user"]
  G2["Pub/Sub · Vertex AI user<br/>portal write<br/>email send <i>via gateway only</i>"]
  G3["Clean bucket, <b>read only</b><br/>findings write<br/>Vertex AI user"]
  G4["Firestore read · score write<br/>Vertex AI user"]
  G5["Pub/Sub publish<br/>outbound fetch <i>via gateway</i><br/>re-review task write"]

  D1["email send · Storage read<br/>approval write"]
  D2["findings write<br/>Storage read"]
  D3["<b>any</b> network egress · email<br/>quarantine bucket"]
  D4["external calls<br/>approvals write"]
  D5["approvals · email<br/>vendor data write"]

  SA1 --> G1
  SA2 --> G2
  SA3 --> G3
  SA4 --> G4
  SA5 --> G5
  SA1 -. "never granted" .-> D1
  SA2 -. "never granted" .-> D2
  SA3 -. "never granted" .-> D3
  SA4 -. "never granted" .-> D4
  SA5 -. "never granted" .-> D5

  SVC["<b>Plus three service identities</b> — vendor portal, dashboard and binder,<br/>inbox simulator. None of them can call a model or write a finding."]
  TEST["<b>tests/test_iam_boundaries.py</b><br/>attempts one denied action per agent and asserts it fails.<br/>A test that fails as expected is a feature — screenshot it."]
  WHY["<b>Why it is load-bearing</b><br/>a fleet holding one god-credential is a single injection away<br/>from disaster. Least privilege is what makes the screening story<br/>true end to end — the agent that reads evidence cannot email,<br/>and the agent that emails cannot touch internal data."]

  FLEET -.-> SVC
  D3 --> TEST
  TEST -.-> WHY

